      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In 1952, Clarence Agress performed an experiment on dogs to demonstrate his idea that a thrombus in a coronary artery could be dissolved without harm to the myocardium. Although this landmark in cardiology has been forgotten, credit to Agress is deserved."},
